    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d890">

                <pb facs="1022" n="928" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg928"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. Terrell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-11-13"><hi rendition="#italic">November 13,
                        1896.</hi></date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1187.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On the 7th instant Moustapha Bey handed to
                    me a translation of a telegraphed memorandum which he had received from the
                    Ottoman foreign office in regard to, first, the inspection of foreign vessels in
                    Turkish ports and the prevention of the landing of persons alleged to be
                    disaffected toward the Ottoman Government, to which end the cooperation of the
                    United States representatives is suggested; and secondly, the prevention of
                    revolutionary publications in the United States and the expulsion of Armenian
                    agitators.</p>
                <p>For your information I inclose a copy both of the memorandum as translated and my
                    reply.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
